  "name": "merge-contributor-pr",
  "description": "Take a contributor's pull request that cannot be merged as-is — usually a conflict with main — resolve the blocker without rewriting their commits, and merge it with a merge commit so their authorship survives. Detects the case where the conflict exists because the same feature already landed through another PR, and closes it as superseded (a credit-only merge only on request) instead of merging a no-op. Use when the user wants a PR fixed up and merged while keeping the original author's commits.",
